Command execution and metadata publication

Status: proposal approved by the user; implementation not started. All tasks below remain open.
Source: [approved proposal](Rendering.CommandPublication.Proposal.md).
Inherited contracts: [resource design](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.Proposal.md),
[inventory](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.Inventory.md), [API coverage](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.ApiCoverage.md).
Evidence: [per-method analysis](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.Analysis.md).
Parent: [resource-handles checklist](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.todo), Phase 4f (delegating phase).

Goal
  Manager creation methods consume assignment-tracked initialization records and return nullable
  canonical metadata plus a success-only handle. Explicit StateCache command methods own native
  dispatch and completion. Lookup, acquisition/recovery and result publication have separate contracts.
  Preserve established facts; query only unknown or driver-derived results and necessary verification.

Scope and ordering
  This checklist is the authoritative implementation sequence delegated by parent Phase 4f.
  The parent records architectural approval and gates later consumer integration on this entire checklist.
  Phase 1 owns remaining contract decisions; Phase 2 repairs bindings; Phases 3–7 implement creation,
  publication and acquisition; Phase 8 handles supplied-metadata preparation; Phase 9 qualifies the whole.
  Parent phase markers are not prerequisites for individual child phases or separate implementation tasks.
  Completion evidence lives here; parent consumer/integrated qualification remains later.
  No recording/queues, GpuCommand/GpuCommandList implementation, StateCache rename, new lifetime keys,
  second registry, full VAO mirror, content tracking or broader interception coverage is introduced.
  Retain GL/Core, Ext and Arb coverage and existing legacy/auxiliary-owner exclusions.
  Higher-level growth, streaming, sampling and content policy stays with existing wrappers/helpers.

Open decisions
  Command-family success evidence remains to be agreed: supplied values and nonthrowing calls do not
  prove acceptance. Nullable results represent reported failure without swallowing required exceptions.
  The exact creation-to-wrapper association handoff remains to be settled before implementation.
  Initialization properties/defaults must be specified per family; record names alone do not settle them.

Phase 1: Settle creation and command-result contracts
  Sources: proposal, Initialization records, Separate three operations, Command execution, Transactions;
  analysis, Binding paths, Native observation pairs and acquisition/reader findings; inherited contracts.
  Outcome: concrete contracts permit implementation without hidden acceptance or ownership assumptions.

  ☐ For every API coverage family and analyzed observer, specify established argument-derived facts,
    required targeted verification, driver-derived reads and unknown-state recovery. Distinguish managed
    commands from arbitrary intercepted calls, including rejected and partially successful multi-calls.
    Preserve native errors; no blanket GetError consumption or blanket Is-object queries.
  ☐ Agree this result policy with the user before implementing it. Record resolved decisions in the
    proposal; architecture approval alone does not settle this policy.
  ☐ Define each initialization record's legal inputs, automatic private assignment mask, required values,
    conditional GL defaults, explicit creation-policy defaults and derivable outputs. Reject missing
    required allocation inputs instead of attempting to query them. Explicit zero/false differs from omission.
  ☐ Specify nullable metadata plus out GpuResourceHandle success/failure semantics and the wrapper handoff:
    manager-owned association and HandleMetadataChanged delivery, no wrapper snapshot assignment,
    no leaked handle between creation and association, and cleanup of provisional state on handoff failure.
    Preserve generated-name versus realized-object and context-free declaration contracts.
  ☐ Specify internal operation/group/deferred state: original entry/context capture, exactly-once completion,
    affected availability, nested/alias grouping, interruption and recovery. Define context-local execution
    through the existing static manager path without a second registry or wrapper tracking state machine.
  ☐ Reconcile proposal/inventory/API mechanics with this approved refinement. Retain the parent consumer
    gate without duplicating implementation tasks; record alternatives and reasons
    already described in the proposal rather than silently retaining the old full-refresh contract.
  ☐ Completion: remaining decisions are explicit, the result policy is agreed, source contracts agree,
    and tasks below have no unresolved foundational prerequisite. No runtime change is required here.

Phase 2: Centralize selector execution and repair binding knowledge
  Depends on Phase 1. Sources: proposal Command execution; analysis Binding paths and Scopes;
  API selector/routing semantics.
  Outcome: acquisition can rely on correct binding scopes without unnecessary result rediscovery.

  ☐ Refactor UseProgramBinding, BindVertexArray and BindProgramPipeline into self-contained execution
    paths under the agreed policy. Preserve managed equal suppression and full-program stage semantics.
  ☐ Repair BindBuffer(ElementArrayBuffer), VertexArrayElementBuffer and external buffer/vertex/program
    selection observation. Maintain per-VAO EBO facts independently of VAO revision notifications.
  ☐ Repair GpuVertexAttribBinding constructors, BindVertexBuffer, SetDivisor and RequireCurrentFacts:
    keep established helper results, preserve stale-copy and original-owner checks, recover only unknown
    fields. Do not introduce a full VAO layout mirror or weaken non-DSA stale-helper rejection.
  ☐ Repair BindFramebufferScope capture to use known independent read/draw selections. Review
    BindScopeTracker, BindBufferScope, BindTextureScope and CaptureBoundaryBindings restoration against
    the same policy. Correct TryGetBufferBindingQuery's AtomicCounterBuffer binding token with a named enum.
  ☐ Migrate selector/routing adapters to shared execution bookkeeping while preserving exact overloads,
    actual external dispatch, errors, reentrancy and unknown-state recovery. Keep read/draw routing distinct.
  ☐ Have subagents verify changed/equal/unknown/rejected bindings, external changes, DSA/fallback,
    scopes, deletion/name reuse and helper revisions. Compare query/bind counts with analysis receipts.
    Run affected builds/tests and canonical package checks; second-review and independently audit this binding increment.
  ☐ Completion: binding restoration and metadata notifications remain correct; verified binding/query
    baseline is available for subsequent acquisition work. No performance inference from counts alone.

Phase 3: Establish manager creation and publication machinery
  Depends on Phase 2. Sources: proposal Responsibilities, Initialization and Transactions; inventory
  manager API, publication and lifecycle contracts. Outcome: one reusable creation/publication boundary.

  ☐ Separate available lookup from native acquire/recover and established-result publication in
    AcquireResource, AcquireWrapperMetadata, ObserveWrapperMetadata, PublishObservedMetadata,
    RefreshMetadata and PublishMetadata. Remove default forced-refresh ambiguity without bypassing
    genuinely unavailable state. Preserve canonical revisions, original association and weak recipients.
  ☐ Implement the agreed initialization-record conventions and nullable creation result/handle protocol.
    Canonical structs remain output-only and flag-free; setters track intent automatically. Empty records
    and non-null empty metadata are valid where the resource has no optional inputs/represented facts.
  ☐ Implement manager-owned creation commit, association and typed snapshot delivery, including local tools.
    Failure cleans newly owned native objects/provisional entries, clears the output handle and leaves
    borrowed dependencies intact. Preserve required exceptions, ownership, detach and retirement behavior.
  ☐ Move begin/complete pairing inside explicit command methods where execution is immediate. Capture
    original identity only where needed; simple selectors do not require heap transaction objects.
    Introduce no mandatory per-call closure allocations or generic string/reflection dispatch.
  ☐ Coordinate grouped initialization/updates by original manager entry, not individual wrapper. Suppress
    repeated acquisition and double publication across aliases; publish coherent results only. Interrupted
    groups leave affected facts unavailable while preserving unrelated established facts.
  ☐ Have subagents verify assignment masks, omission/zero/false, conditional defaults, nullable success and
    failure, handoff failure, cleanup, alias groups, reentrancy, context retirement and exactly-once delivery.
  ☐ Completion: the common boundary is verified; family migrations can use it without inventing their
    own acquisition, publication or failure protocols. Existing consumers remain functional during migration.

Phase 4: Migrate buffer and image creation and mutations
  Depends on Phase 3. Sources: proposal Resource coverage; analysis readers/observers; API B1, T1–T4, R1, I1.
  Each task includes input/default definition, accepted-result publication, failure cleanup and call-site migration.

  ☐ Implement GpuBufferInitialization -> GpuBufferMetadata for GpuBufferObject, GpuVbo, GpuEbo,
    GpuUniformBuffer, GpuShaderStorageBuffer, GpuAtomicCounterBuffer, GpuIndirectBuffer,
    GpuPixelPackBuffer and GpuPixelUnpackBuffer. Keep GpuBufferUploader's role and DSA/fallback dispatch;
    remove RegisterBufferWrapper's duplicate validity reads without treating reserved names as realized.
  ☐ Implement GpuTextureInitialization -> GpuTextureMetadata for GpuTexture, Texture2D, Texture3D,
    DynamicTexture2D, DynamicTexture3D, DynamicTextureCube, DepthTexture, StencilTexture,
    DepthStencilTexture, PmjJitterTexture and CloudBlueNoiseTexture. Preserve constructor inputs,
    allocation choices and GpuLimits use. Derive established mip/face facts as GpuTextureLevelMetadata.
  ☐ Implement GpuRenderbufferInitialization -> GpuRenderbufferMetadata for GpuRenderbuffer.
    Preserve driver-derived actual sample counts and capability-specific storage semantics.
  ☐ Implement GpuBufferTextureInitialization -> GpuTextureMetadata for GpuBufferView/GpuBufferTexture,
    constructing GpuTextureBufferMetadata centrally. Preserve whole-buffer versus explicit-range semantics,
    native-width ranges, alignment, backing identity and dependency propagation.
  ☐ Implement GpuTextureViewInitialization -> GpuTextureMetadata for GpuTextureView, constructing
    GpuTextureViewMetadata centrally. Preserve source identity/storage revision and view-relative levels.
    Keep renderbuffer-backed texture associations on GpuTextureMetadata/GpuRenderbufferMetadata.
  ☐ Migrate buffer/renderbuffer/texture storage, parameter, mip-generation and association command observers
    to shared execution/publication. Update only affected fields; preserve native acceptance, interruption
    and imported-storage semantics. Base/max changes must not scan unrelated storage; immutable content-only
    mip generation must not invent storage changes. Review ObserveBufferView, TryObserveBufferAssociation,
    ConfigureTextureView and RefreshGeneratedTextureMetadata against this rule.
  ☐ Have subagents verify every migrated family's creation, replacement, failed allocation, defaults,
    output metadata, dependencies and DSA/fallback paths. Compare native queries to the binding-corrected
    baseline; separate required verification/sample reads from eliminated descriptor rediscovery.
  ☐ Completion: all listed wrappers use manager creation, no wrapper authors canonical snapshots,
    and narrow image/buffer mutations no longer cause unrelated full reads.

Phase 5: Migrate framebuffer and executable resource creation and publication
  Depends on Phase 4. Sources: proposal coverage/command examples; API F1/P1; analysis corresponding findings.

  ☐ Implement GpuFramebufferInitialization -> GpuFramebufferMetadata for GpuFramebuffer,
    DynamicGpuFramebuffer and StaticGpuFramebuffer. Construct GpuFramebufferImageMetadata centrally;
    keep attachment ownership/static locks, proven multiview semantics and independent routing intact.
  ☐ Refactor RequireNativeAttachment, ObserveFramebufferAttachment, BindFramebufferResource,
    PublishRenderPassMetadata, GpuFramebufferAttachmentDiscovery.Read and ReconcileAttachmentMetadata
    to avoid targeted verification followed by a full scan. Coordinate attachment groups and dependencies.
    GpuFramebufferAttachment receives projected GpuImageMetadata; owned backing uses Phase 4 creation.
    Default framebuffer/surface metadata retains its separate publication path.
  ☐ Implement GpuShaderInitialization -> GpuShaderMetadata for GpuShaderModule: retain established fixed
    stage without rediscovery; compilation/binary loading retains its existing success/lifetime boundary.
  ☐ Implement GpuProgramInitialization -> GpuProgramMetadata for GpuProgramObject/GpuComputePipeline.
    Fresh creation publishes an empty executable without reflection. Preserve GpuProgram/GpuComputeProgram
    composition and existing deferred linking. AcquireCreatedProgramMetadata and AcquireProgramMetadata
    follow separate creation versus discovery contracts.
  ☐ Keep explicit pending identity/context for SubmitProgramLink/CompleteProgramLink behavior. Acquire
    GpuProgramResourceMetadata and GpuProgramTextureUnitMetadata when executable results require it;
    unit/block changes update affected facts without full interface reflection. Preserve unsupported-bindless
    withdrawal, prepared-layout invalidation, full-stage selection and owner-controlled re-preparation.
  ☐ Have subagents verify attachment groups/modes, failed/rejected commands, actual link outcomes,
    deferred retirement/name reuse, unit/block updates, empty programs and unchanged render-pass facts.
  ☐ Completion: framebuffer and executable creation/update paths satisfy canonical publication with
    targeted acquisition and existing ownership, validation and preparation boundaries intact.

Phase 6: Migrate remaining resource creation families
  Depends on Phase 5. Sources: proposal Resource coverage; inventory per-kind schemas and lifecycle.
  Each family uses the Phase 3 protocol, legal inputs only, nullable output and failure cleanup.

  ☐ GpuVao: GpuVertexArrayInitialization -> GpuVertexArrayMetadata; preserve empty revision schema.
  ☐ GpuProgramPipeline: GpuProgramPipelineInitialization -> GpuProgramPipelineMetadata.
  ☐ GpuSampler: GpuSamplerInitialization -> GpuSamplerMetadata; retain authored sampling policy.
  ☐ GpuQuery: GpuQueryInitialization -> GpuQueryMetadata; GpuTimerQuery/GpuTimestampQuery remain composition.
  ☐ GpuFence: GpuSyncInitialization -> GpuSyncMetadata; preserve pointer-width identity and wait semantics.
  ☐ GpuTransformFeedback: GpuTransformFeedbackInitialization -> GpuTransformFeedbackMetadata.
  ☐ GpuSemaphore: GpuSemaphoreInitialization -> GpuSemaphoreMetadata; preserve import ownership.
  ☐ GpuMemoryObject: GpuMemoryObjectInitialization -> GpuMemoryObjectMetadata; preserve import ownership.
  ☐ Keep empty metadata empty; do not add queries or persistent fields to justify initialization records.
    GpuVertexAttribBinding remains a helper with no additional canonical struct.
  ☐ Have subagents verify creation/failure/cleanup and retained metadata/lifetime semantics per family;
    exercise native capability paths where available and explicitly record unexecuted capability cases.
  ☐ Completion: all proposal creation families are migrated and no generic wrapper metadata tracking exists.

Phase 7: Finish external acquisition, recovery and adapter migration
  Depends on Phase 6. Sources: complete analysis method inventory; proposal lookup/acquire/publication;
  inventory association/dependency contracts and API coverage. Outcome: acquisition repairs are ready for audit.

  ☐ Reconcile AcquireExternalImageTexture, AcquireImageMetadata, AcquireBufferTextureBacking,
    AcquireRenderbufferTextureBacking, AssociateImageResource and AssignImageMetadata. Reuse available
    covered entries for raw aliases; keep image projection query-free and retain original backing identity.
  ☐ Migrate BorrowedTexture and external texture/renderbuffer/framebuffer/shader/program wrap/adopt paths
    to lookup or acquisition without creation-time mutation. Unsupported external changes retain explicit
    invalidation/recovery; registry membership alone does not certify observation coverage.
  ☐ Reconcile GpuBufferMetadataReader, GpuTextureMetadataReader, GpuRenderbufferMetadataReader,
    GpuRenderbufferTextureMetadataReader, GpuFramebufferMetadataReader, GpuShaderMetadataReader and
    GpuProgramMetadataReader: preserve unknown-state discovery while narrowing result reads. Avoid repeat
    context-local reads when established results suffice, without trusting stale snapshots after failure.
  ☐ Reconcile every remaining BeginNative*/Complete observer in the analysis with immediate internal
    execution, grouped or deferred handling. Migrate exact compiler-checked adapters; preserve each allowed
    overload, external dispatch/error behavior, per-object failure and no-content-only metadata work.
  ☐ Review CompleteResourceDeletion/WasResourceDeleted query policy separately from acquisition under
    Phase 1's contract. Preserve retained shader/program deletion semantics and old-association safety.
  ☐ Reconcile every analysis row with an implemented disposition and evidence; remove superseded forced
    refresh paths, redundant checks and caller-managed pairing. Preserve required discovery and recovery.
  ☐ Have subagents verify available/raw-alias/unknown/unavailable/local-tool scenarios, dependent invalidation,
    failed commands, context loss, name reuse, supported adapters and binding-preserving fallback readers.
    Run affected regressions/package checks, second-review and independently audit acquisition repairs.
  ☐ Completion: all analyzed methods have verified dispositions; no foundation repair is deferred to consumers.

Phase 8: Require supplied metadata for binding preparation
  Depends on Phase 7. Sources: proposal Decisions and acceptance; Rendering.ShaderBindingState.md,
  Prepared resource submission. Supplied-metadata-only preparation is already approved; no new design gate.

  ☐ Make GpuPreparedBindings constructor require GpuProgramMetadata; remove optional/native query paths
    and ReadBlocks reflection, and remove its program-ID parameter if unused. No hidden manager acquisition.
  ☐ Update GpuProgramInterface and all callers to supply available complete metadata. Preserve fixed-slot,
    activity, array, block-size/stage, atomic-counter and authored-contract validation and prepared tables.
  ☐ Update StandaloneNumericInputTests and ReflectionQueries consumers to measure acquisition at its actual
    boundary. Reject unavailable/incomplete facts rather than querying to fill gaps.
  ☐ Have subagents verify valid/incomplete/incompatible snapshots and production preparation with zero
    native acquisition from supplied snapshots. Reconcile current shader-binding docs, run affected
    regressions/package checks, second-review and independently audit preparation.
  ☐ Completion: preparation only validates and prepares supplied facts; no native acquisition fallback remains.

Phase 9: Qualify and reconcile the complete foundation
  Depends on Phase 8. Sources: proposal Decisions and acceptance; parent validation and downstream gates.

  ☐ Freeze candidate source/binary identity. Have subagents run matched native query/bind probes against
    analysis receipts, separating binding recovery, verification, driver discovery, creation and publication.
    Measure allocation/dispatch overhead and check outputs/restored state, not merely reduced query counts.
  ☐ Have subagents run affected suites and canonical build/package verification. Cover failures, interrupted
    groups, aliases, dependencies, deferred work, ownership/disposal/detach, contexts and DSA/fallback paths.
    Report capability gaps explicitly; headless receipts do not establish live appearance or frame time.
  ☐ Remove temporary migration compatibility paths and newly introduced probe scaffolding; retain receipts.
    Coordinate existing ResourceCallObserver removal with parent Phase 6 so its later measurements remain
    possible. No automatic game launch; visual acceptance stays user-run.
  ☐ Reconcile proposal/inventory/API contracts and current architecture documentation with implemented
    behavior. Supply completion evidence for the delegating parent phase; leave consumer, RHI and
    multi-bind work open. Do not mark the parent plan complete on this checklist's completion.
  ☐ Perform a second review and independent completion audit against every proposal requirement, resource
    family and analysis disposition. Resolve required findings before checking completion items.
  ☐ Completion: all approved creation/publication/binding/preparation changes are implemented and verified,
    unresolved evidence limits are explicit and parent consumer work can proceed on the repaired foundation.
